WEBVTT

00:11.950 --> 00:15.410
Welcome to Shirasaza

00:11.950 --> 00:15.410
ahead

00:11.950 --> 00:15.410
B & B

00:17.170 --> 00:19.930
It’s in the lap of nature, and it’s quiet.

00:19.930 --> 00:21.510
The air is clean,

00:21.510 --> 00:23.370
you’ll feel at home,

00:23.590 --> 00:26.190
and the food is fresh and delicious!

00:26.190 --> 00:29.210
The eggs our chickens lay
are especially amazing!

00:30.500 --> 00:35.790
Or so the guests who stay with us say,

00:35.790 --> 00:38.790
but honestly, after living here for 16 years,

00:38.790 --> 00:40.460
I’m almost sick of it!

00:53.990 --> 00:58.210
komorebi no mukougawa de

00:53.990 --> 00:58.210
Behind the veil of sunshine

01:00.500 --> 01:04.880
kimi wa mada kizuitenai no

01:00.500 --> 01:04.880
You haven't realized yet

01:04.880 --> 01:06.880
watashi no koto

01:04.880 --> 01:06.880
That I'm here

01:06.880 --> 01:11.390
karuku te wo futte aizu shite

01:06.880 --> 01:11.390
I wave at you to say hi

01:12.890 --> 01:19.730
kakeyoru dake de ureshiku naru yo

01:12.890 --> 01:19.730
Just running up to you makes me happy

01:19.730 --> 01:26.780
kono mama de iraretara ii na

01:19.730 --> 01:26.780
I wish we could just stay like this

01:26.780 --> 01:32.570
itsumo no sakamichi mo chotto

01:26.780 --> 01:32.570
I'd be so lonely on our usual slope

01:32.570 --> 01:35.330
setsunai no

01:32.570 --> 01:35.330
Otherwise

01:35.910 --> 01:43.420
kirisugita kami ga kaze ni yureru tabi

01:35.910 --> 01:43.420
I cut my hair too short, but the wind still catches it

01:43.420 --> 01:49.300
harikomu yokogao kakushiteru no

01:43.420 --> 01:49.300
I keep watching you from the corner of my eye

01:49.300 --> 01:56.430
taisetsuna ima wo tsumikasanete ikou

01:49.300 --> 01:56.430
Let's pile up all these precious moments

01:56.430 --> 02:00.310
mayou hi mo tanoshii hi mo

01:56.430 --> 02:00.310
All the bad days and the fun days

02:00.310 --> 02:05.360
takaramono ni naru kara

02:00.310 --> 02:05.360
Will become treasures in the future

02:14.860 --> 02:19.530
1st Road
Café Terrace of Winds

02:25.960 --> 02:28.880
Ah, Riecchi! Mornin’!

02:28.880 --> 02:32.860
Hey... Sayo... senpai...

02:32.860 --> 02:34.570
Anri... senpai...

02:34.570 --> 02:37.060
Haruno... senpai...

02:36.170 --> 02:38.760
You’re drenched in sweat again.

02:38.760 --> 02:40.860
I hate this!

02:40.860 --> 02:45.390
I’m the only one riding a bicycle. It’s not fair!

02:45.390 --> 02:48.090
We were in your shoes once.

02:48.090 --> 02:52.230
It was hell for me when I couldn’t get anyone to drive me to school.

02:52.930 --> 02:56.600
Well yeah, you’re a special case, Harunon.

02:57.360 --> 03:00.360
I’ll kiss this miserable lifestyle goodbye

03:00.360 --> 03:03.660
and get my license as soon as I turn 16!

03:03.660 --> 03:08.480
Wait for me until then, my little Zoo-chan!

03:08.480 --> 03:11.150
Yeah, we know you love Zoomers.

03:11.150 --> 03:14.330
Sayo-senpai, it’s not Zoomer. It’s Zoo-chan!

03:14.330 --> 03:16.410
I even have the catalog with me!

03:15.620 --> 03:16.730
We know.

03:16.730 --> 03:19.310
Anri-senpai, Haruno-senpai,
you should look, too!

03:19.310 --> 03:20.670
Isn’t it cute?

03:20.670 --> 03:21.550
What’s wrong, Harunon?

03:21.850 --> 03:24.430
I gotta keep these cool.

03:32.410 --> 03:37.230
It’s just a questionnaire,
so don’t think about it too hard.

03:37.230 --> 03:39.500
Easier said than done.

03:42.840 --> 03:45.000
I’m collecting the papers in three minutes!

03:58.550 --> 04:01.050
Oh, you’re getting a new helper?

04:01.050 --> 04:04.860
Yeah. The peak season is starting soon,
and we don’t want to be short-handed.

04:04.710 --> 04:07.060
You’re awesome today, Zoo-chan!

04:05.330 --> 04:07.000
What kind of a person will it be?

04:07.000 --> 04:08.510
No clue.

04:08.770 --> 04:10.540
I hope it’s someone nice.

04:10.540 --> 04:11.430
Yeah.

04:12.050 --> 04:15.270
How about your standard butler?

04:16.310 --> 04:18.280
No way!

04:18.770 --> 04:20.230
A butler...

04:20.740 --> 04:25.200
Lady Haruno, would you prefer dinner or a bath first?

04:25.450 --> 04:29.910
I’ve finished cleaning, laundry, preparing the
guest rooms, and tending to the chickens.

04:30.500 --> 04:34.870
Please leave your homework and exam preparations to me as well.

04:38.070 --> 04:39.800
The daydream’s over.

04:39.800 --> 04:41.130
Welcome back!

04:41.130 --> 04:43.690
Did you meet an amazing butler?

04:43.690 --> 04:45.840
I did it again!

04:46.370 --> 04:47.800
Anyway, I can’t wait to meet them.

04:48.500 --> 04:50.790
They’ll be gone in no time, though.

04:51.250 --> 04:52.640
As usual.

04:53.400 --> 04:59.610
In the end, they all say, “I could reevaluate myself as I was surrounded by nature,” and quit.

05:00.530 --> 05:02.340
Well, why don’t we go?

05:02.690 --> 05:03.720
Where to?

05:03.720 --> 05:06.160
We should see what kind of a person it is.

05:06.160 --> 05:07.560
To my place?

05:07.560 --> 05:10.200
I’ve gotta text my brother then.

05:10.200 --> 05:11.280
It’s settled!

05:11.280 --> 05:12.760
Seriously?

05:34.790 --> 05:35.800
Wind...

05:38.710 --> 05:40.710
So cool!

05:45.830 --> 05:50.830
She’ll be working here from now on. Her name is Cynthia B. Rogers.

05:50.830 --> 05:53.580
I met her online!

05:55.050 --> 05:57.960
What a bunch of kawaii girls!

05:57.960 --> 05:59.850
What language was that?

05:59.850 --> 06:01.460
A mix of a few.

06:01.460 --> 06:04.510
Excuse me for a moment.

06:04.510 --> 06:07.290
This suit is so tight on my boobs.

06:09.530 --> 06:11.890
That’s much better.

06:11.890 --> 06:15.200
Hey, who owns the CBR in front of th—

06:15.200 --> 06:15.880
Boobs!

06:15.880 --> 06:18.850
Oh, another kawaii girl!

06:19.320 --> 06:21.860
This photo will be good enough to thank my brother.

06:25.780 --> 06:27.340
Indian-style pasta,

06:27.340 --> 06:28.480
in New Yorker arrange,

06:28.480 --> 06:30.710
with Vietnamese topping!

06:30.710 --> 06:32.360
What style is it again?

06:32.820 --> 06:35.530
Well, it’s definitely international.

06:35.530 --> 06:39.830
Cynthia has been to a number of countries on her bike!

06:39.830 --> 06:42.330
That’s so cool!

06:42.330 --> 06:44.340
<i>Douzo, </i>please dig in!

06:44.970 --> 06:46.840
I’ll take you up on your offer...

06:52.350 --> 06:53.720
How is it?

06:53.720 --> 06:54.840
This is...

06:54.840 --> 06:56.380
...quite a dangerous mix.

06:56.380 --> 06:57.800
A whole new experience!

06:57.800 --> 07:01.100
I–I can eat it if I try hard! Maybe.

07:02.980 --> 07:07.030
Due to popular demand,
I’m making another course!

07:08.180 --> 07:09.240
What’s this?

07:09.240 --> 07:10.990
Rice with egg.

07:11.430 --> 07:14.020
You’re supposed to mix it up.

07:15.810 --> 07:18.970
Mix-mix-mix!

07:21.910 --> 07:24.710
It’s super good!

07:24.930 --> 07:26.090
Really?

07:27.790 --> 07:33.760
Nippon’s food is just wonderful! It moves me to tears!

07:33.760 --> 07:35.360
You like it <i>that</i> much?

07:35.360 --> 07:36.510
Haruno, you’re a god!

07:36.510 --> 07:38.220
Not at all...

07:58.870 --> 08:00.330
Cynthia, huh?

08:02.920 --> 08:05.120
She sure is more than I can chew.

08:05.120 --> 08:08.120
It’s not like she’s
a bad person or anything.

08:09.190 --> 08:13.300
She just doesn’t fit in this tiny village.

08:13.770 --> 08:15.640
Unlike me.

08:20.530 --> 08:21.770
Hey, Haruno!

08:23.230 --> 08:24.690
I’m coming!

08:25.050 --> 08:28.080
C–Cynthia? What are you doing here?

08:28.080 --> 08:30.650
Your mom told me you’d be here!

08:32.450 --> 08:34.110
Great!

08:34.660 --> 08:38.890
Grilled eel!

08:47.400 --> 08:48.710
Pretty good.

08:49.010 --> 08:52.730
This was my only spot
where I could be alone.

08:52.730 --> 08:54.360
Thanks a lot, Mom...

08:54.360 --> 08:56.220
Haruno, you’re amazing.

08:56.950 --> 08:59.830
This tea, this great view,

09:00.310 --> 09:02.040
and the rice with egg...

09:02.390 --> 09:05.770
You’ve showed me three wonderful new things in just one day.

09:05.770 --> 09:09.440
No, that doesn’t make me amazing at all.

09:09.440 --> 09:13.280
In fact, you having been to so many countries is much more amazing.

09:13.280 --> 09:15.480
You want to go, too?

09:15.480 --> 09:17.180
No! I can’t!

09:17.180 --> 09:19.020
You can’t? Why?

09:19.020 --> 09:20.870
Why?

09:21.460 --> 09:23.450
There are some things you just can’t do.

09:25.650 --> 09:27.980
There are things I just can’t do?

09:28.730 --> 09:33.310
When did I start to think like that?

09:33.310 --> 09:34.280
Haruno.

09:35.080 --> 09:36.250
What?

09:36.790 --> 09:39.300
Can I have another ippai of ocha?

09:39.970 --> 09:43.290
Ah, you want another? Sure, okay.

09:45.330 --> 09:48.340
And the road is straight
as far as you can see!

09:49.910 --> 09:52.480
There are no houses around either.

09:52.480 --> 09:54.670
I heard that the American Midwest is really like that.

09:54.670 --> 09:57.150
Wow! That sounds good!

09:57.320 --> 10:00.490
But then the sun set.

10:00.490 --> 10:01.960
And then? And then?

10:01.960 --> 10:04.970
I thought I should set up camp there.

10:04.970 --> 10:07.790
Then the wolves
started howling like...

10:07.790 --> 10:08.580
Scary!

10:08.580 --> 10:11.120
It was really lots of fun!

10:11.120 --> 10:12.750
That was fun?!

10:12.750 --> 10:16.590
Playing tag on your bike with wolves is fun!

10:16.590 --> 10:18.440
Lots of fun!

10:20.610 --> 10:23.860
The wide world outside, huh?

10:33.520 --> 10:35.940
It always ends like this.

10:36.860 --> 10:38.620
I can’t do it.

10:38.620 --> 10:40.320
It’s impossible.

10:44.090 --> 10:49.520
Then just a bit from the other side, the raft started to sink!

10:49.520 --> 10:52.950
I had to jump with all my might or I’d sink!

10:55.860 --> 10:57.900
Even if it seems impossible, I have to try!

11:03.240 --> 11:04.470
Yep, she’s back.

11:04.470 --> 11:05.830
Haruno?

11:05.830 --> 11:07.400
Don’t worry about it.

11:07.400 --> 11:08.980
She’s just daydreaming, as usual.

11:09.800 --> 11:12.490
Not again...

11:12.490 --> 11:13.940
No worries.

11:15.250 --> 11:18.280
I’ll go abroad just like Cynthia!

11:18.280 --> 11:19.650
Yes you can!

11:19.880 --> 11:22.870
I’ll go to the ends of Earth with Zoo-chan!

11:24.360 --> 11:27.030
What’s this feeling?

11:27.860 --> 11:32.330
I know there are some things
I just can’t achieve.

11:33.320 --> 11:37.590
What I can<i> do must
be something minor.</i>

11:38.070 --> 11:42.060
Getting away from this place won’t help too much, either.

11:42.060 --> 11:46.230
Wait, am I jealous?

11:47.880 --> 11:50.360
That’s so petty.

12:03.010 --> 12:05.980
I’ve been feeling sluggish
since the morning.

12:05.980 --> 12:08.430
It must be because of the dream I had.

12:06.990 --> 12:12.560
Shirasaza Tomoba

12:08.430 --> 12:11.100
Sayo won the Nobel Prize in Literature.

12:11.100 --> 12:13.260
Aa-chan had become a famous composer.

12:13.260 --> 12:17.100
Riecchi was flying the sky
on some giant bike.

12:17.100 --> 12:20.600
And I was delivering them eggs.

12:20.600 --> 12:22.170
I don’t get it!

12:23.850 --> 12:28.620
Because of Cynthia,
my everyday life got a bit livelier,

12:28.620 --> 12:33.320
but these past few days
have been eventless.

12:34.900 --> 12:38.600
Haruno, I’ll do it properly
this time! Just watch!

12:38.600 --> 12:39.920
Okay, okay.

12:39.920 --> 12:42.170
Good morning, ladies!

12:42.170 --> 12:43.150
I’ve come for your eggs.

12:43.150 --> 12:45.920
Stop! Stop! Stop!

12:45.920 --> 12:48.540
Don’t think you can get away with this!

12:58.280 --> 13:00.860
Is this all you’ve got, chickens?!

13:00.860 --> 13:01.720
Come on!

13:01.720 --> 13:04.760
Cynthia, I’m kinda in a hurry.

13:04.760 --> 13:05.880
Ah, sorry.

13:06.250 --> 13:08.890
Take care, Haruno!

13:08.890 --> 13:12.970
That’s how it is.
If anything has changed,

13:12.970 --> 13:15.930
it’s the fact that I’ve got
even more work to do.

13:25.950 --> 13:29.260
It’s not funny, Aa-chan!

13:29.260 --> 13:30.660
My bad! My bad!

13:30.660 --> 13:32.990
She’s still new here.

13:32.990 --> 13:34.720
She’ll get used to things eventually.

13:34.720 --> 13:36.070
Yeah.

13:37.160 --> 13:41.030
She doesn’t seem to be a bad person,
so just think of it as helping someone.

13:43.840 --> 13:50.270
Zoo-chan is the best, but to travel around the world, I’ll need a bigger bike!

13:50.270 --> 13:52.100
But still...

13:52.500 --> 13:54.460
The bike shop Motoya.

13:54.460 --> 13:58.950
People in the area come here to
buy bikes and get them repaired.

13:59.540 --> 14:02.840
We’ve known about it since we were kids,

14:02.840 --> 14:05.240
it’s close to the school,

14:05.240 --> 14:09.020
and it even has a cafe where
we can just hang out.

14:09.020 --> 14:12.920
So the four of us somehow
always end up here after school.

14:13.950 --> 14:16.730
Riecchi, are you serious
about traveling around the world?

14:16.730 --> 14:17.660
Yes!

14:17.660 --> 14:18.910
Of course!

14:18.910 --> 14:22.760
Doesn’t it sound wonderful?
Crossing America by bike!

14:23.950 --> 14:27.450
Yeah! It’s gotta be with Zoo-chan!

14:28.390 --> 14:30.700
You’re fine with playing tag with wolves?

14:31.800 --> 14:34.660
Oh yeah. Then a bigger one would be...

14:34.660 --> 14:37.400
No! I must believe in Zoo-chan.

14:37.400 --> 14:39.960
Just forget about it. It’s impossible!

14:39.960 --> 14:42.640
You were just influenced too much by Cynthia!

14:42.640 --> 14:45.230
I’m not the only one. Look.

14:45.420 --> 14:48.400
Indeed. As a matter of fact, I am too.

14:48.400 --> 14:49.200
This.

14:52.410 --> 14:53.580
Even Sayo-chan...

14:53.580 --> 14:56.910
See? You should be honest with yourself, Haruno-senpai.

14:58.110 --> 15:00.790
Honest, huh? Guess you’re right.

15:01.940 --> 15:03.660
What is it?

15:03.660 --> 15:06.030
Want to hear the song
I made yesterday?

15:06.030 --> 15:08.500
I do! I do!

15:09.050 --> 15:12.280
Featuring my dear puppy Maro! Enjoy!

15:12.280 --> 15:14.490
Maro!

15:19.030 --> 15:21.290
Maro’s rhythm is perfect!

15:21.290 --> 15:22.270
Yeah.

15:22.450 --> 15:24.520
He’s a genius!

15:24.520 --> 15:26.720
Are you listening at all?

15:26.720 --> 15:27.990
We are!

15:29.140 --> 15:32.170
It feels different from usual.

15:32.170 --> 15:36.540
I got my inspiration from
listening to Cynthia’s stories.

15:36.540 --> 15:37.770
Even you, Aa-chan?

15:37.770 --> 15:42.940
Yeah. Her stories leave
an impression, don’t they?

15:44.100 --> 15:49.390
But isn’t it a bit too cute for
something based off Cynthia’s stories?

15:49.390 --> 15:51.760
You just don’t get it, do you?

15:52.120 --> 15:55.720
You need to go for something unexpected to hit it big!

15:56.020 --> 15:59.440
Like how the fact that Kinko-san and
Ginko-san were beauties long ago

15:59.440 --> 16:00.810
makes them so unique today!

16:00.810 --> 16:02.440
“Hit it big”?

16:02.920 --> 16:04.330
Anyway,

16:04.330 --> 16:07.590
I’ll be counting on you to sing
when the song gets finished, Haruno!

16:08.200 --> 16:10.360
Exclusive singer for Anri-senpai!

16:10.360 --> 16:12.670
Me again?

16:12.670 --> 16:15.820
Why can’t you just sing it yourself with Maro?

16:15.820 --> 16:17.660
No. The singer must be Haruno.

16:17.660 --> 16:19.160
That’s the rule!

16:19.450 --> 16:25.500
You were the youngest ever to win the Cool Breeze Singing Contest!

16:26.380 --> 16:29.340
Go! Don’t lose to Maro, Haruno-senpai!

16:29.340 --> 16:31.040
Aim for a U.S. debut!

16:31.040 --> 16:33.340
You can sing a global hit!

16:32.050 --> 16:35.080
Stop it! It’s embarrassing!

16:35.700 --> 16:37.850
Sorry about all the noise.

16:38.790 --> 16:43.310
If you think it’s embarrassing, does that mean you actually dream about it?

16:43.310 --> 16:45.000
No, it doesn’t!

16:47.560 --> 16:50.730
Back in the day, you always talked about how you’d become a singer.

16:50.730 --> 16:52.040
Stop it.

16:52.040 --> 16:54.570
And how the singing contest
was your first step to success!

16:54.570 --> 16:56.800
Stop it already!

16:56.800 --> 16:59.410
That’s something
I’m trying to forget!

16:59.670 --> 17:04.180
Besides, who’d want to listen to me sing in these mountains anyway?

17:04.180 --> 17:05.460
I would!

17:09.930 --> 17:13.310
I’ve covered a lot of ground
with this, so please give it a look!

17:13.310 --> 17:15.180
It’s in great condition.

17:15.700 --> 17:18.680
I make sure to give it
a checkup every day!

17:18.820 --> 17:20.430
Cynthia-san!

17:20.650 --> 17:22.640
Hey, girls!

17:22.640 --> 17:25.600
Cynthia-san, come have tea with us!

17:25.600 --> 17:28.110
Sounds good! I’ll join you!

17:28.110 --> 17:29.930
Stop!

17:30.490 --> 17:32.300
Don’t do that outside!

17:34.500 --> 17:36.960
Just to warn you before we start,

17:36.960 --> 17:40.200
something unbelievably cute will be onscreen.

17:40.200 --> 17:40.780
Okay.

17:41.060 --> 17:43.760
Telling you to not make a sound would be pointless,

17:43.760 --> 17:44.990
so you get three seconds.

17:44.990 --> 17:47.180
After that, concentrate on the song.

17:47.180 --> 17:48.120
Okay.

17:48.120 --> 17:49.850
Here you go.

17:52.170 --> 17:54.700
One... Two... Three.

17:52.170 --> 17:56.880
So cute!

17:54.700 --> 17:55.750
Okay, time’s up!

18:03.830 --> 18:05.610
It’s super wonderful!

18:05.610 --> 18:06.570
All right!

18:06.570 --> 18:08.090
She likes it!

18:08.090 --> 18:10.540
This is the passport to the world!

18:10.540 --> 18:12.090
You made this, Anri?

18:12.090 --> 18:13.000
That’s right.

18:13.000 --> 18:15.670
And Haruno-senpai is gonna sing!

18:17.350 --> 18:19.200
Can I listen again when it’s done?

18:19.200 --> 18:20.070
Of course!

18:21.930 --> 18:24.660
What are they so excited over?

18:24.810 --> 18:26.540
Hey, Cynthia-san!

18:26.540 --> 18:29.850
Where should I go on my first bike trip?

18:29.850 --> 18:31.630
You should go where you want!

18:31.990 --> 18:33.540
Where I want? But...

18:35.350 --> 18:37.590
That doesn’t sound like it’ll be easy.

18:38.530 --> 18:41.790
You’ll be fine! You can do it!

18:41.790 --> 18:44.780
Even if you just ride your bike without a destination,

18:44.780 --> 18:47.000
you can encounter plenty of
wonderful things along the way!

18:47.000 --> 18:48.760
Really?!

18:50.040 --> 18:51.720
Try first!

18:51.720 --> 18:52.720
Yes!

18:53.320 --> 18:55.070
Don’t be so irresponsible!

18:58.310 --> 19:01.120
We’re different from Cynthia.

19:01.120 --> 19:02.330
In what way?

19:02.330 --> 19:06.040
Well... in the way we were raised, and how we think.

19:06.370 --> 19:07.500
Don’t forget size.

19:07.500 --> 19:11.180
That’s right! Cynthia is from Australia,

19:11.180 --> 19:13.960
and we’re from this tiny town!

19:13.960 --> 19:15.460
The scale is totally different.

19:15.880 --> 19:20.040
If she’s a typical motorbike,
we’re scooters!

19:20.710 --> 19:23.440
There are some things we just can’t do.

19:23.440 --> 19:28.270
Yeah, but what’s wrong with Riecchi blabbering about her dreams?

19:28.270 --> 19:30.060
Yeah!

19:30.060 --> 19:36.840
And if you said your daydreams aloud, maybe they’d turn real!

19:36.840 --> 19:37.780
As if.

19:39.810 --> 19:43.130
My singing won’t go any further than the singing contest.

19:44.330 --> 19:49.400
Sorry, but I’ve gotta take home
the veggies I got in the morning.

19:50.440 --> 19:53.600
Cynthia, you’ll be here until your bike’s ready, right?

19:53.600 --> 19:54.890
Yes, that’s right.

19:54.890 --> 19:58.270
Then I’m going ahead.
See you all later!

19:58.270 --> 19:59.160
Bye-bye!

19:59.160 --> 20:00.170
Later!

20:16.890 --> 20:22.830
Mister, that bike can go a lot
farther than my Giorno, right?

20:22.830 --> 20:26.230
That depends on the person riding it.

20:27.320 --> 20:29.680
So the problem is me?

20:29.680 --> 20:33.080
Something happened between you and this beauty’s owner?

20:33.080 --> 20:35.960
It’s not like Cynthia’s in the wrong.

20:36.420 --> 20:40.600
It’s probably my fault
that we can’t get along.

20:41.160 --> 20:44.180
I’m too petty.

20:47.410 --> 20:51.520
New parts always make
the machine jerky at first.

20:52.820 --> 20:54.720
Don’t worry about it.

20:54.720 --> 20:57.450
Take your time and
get used to each other.

20:57.450 --> 21:00.230
I wonder...

21:08.970 --> 21:12.160
They’re all too easily
influenced by Cynthia.

21:12.160 --> 21:17.560
Is this the difference
in a person’s scale?

21:17.560 --> 21:19.700
Hey, Haruno!

21:22.090 --> 21:24.550
I saw this coming.

21:25.610 --> 21:27.760
Miso oden!

21:32.720 --> 21:36.010
Haruno, I have something
cool to show you.

21:36.010 --> 21:36.980
Right here!

21:37.250 --> 21:39.280
That’s Maro!

21:39.280 --> 21:40.860
You went to Aa-chan’s?

21:40.860 --> 21:42.440
Oh, yes!

21:50.150 --> 21:52.160
I brought a cup for myself today.

21:52.160 --> 21:53.830
That’s for noodles, though.

21:53.830 --> 21:55.210
Thanks.

22:04.070 --> 22:06.340
You never know unless you try.

22:07.640 --> 22:10.550
What? You came here just to say that?

22:10.550 --> 22:12.010
No!

22:12.010 --> 22:13.310
You’re the one who said it.

22:15.410 --> 22:18.220
Sayo, Anri, and Rie told me.

22:18.220 --> 22:21.570
They said you used to say it all the time.

22:26.230 --> 22:27.910
What are you getting at?

22:28.980 --> 22:30.950
Haruno, let’s go to the sea!

22:34.130 --> 22:36.200
Yes, the sea! Just the two of us!

22:36.580 --> 22:39.210
What’s with you all of a sudden? When?

22:39.210 --> 22:40.460
Tonight!

22:41.460 --> 22:42.940
What are you saying?!

22:42.940 --> 22:44.010
It’s okay!

22:44.010 --> 22:47.530
No! My parents would worry!

22:51.770 --> 22:53.610
Take care!

22:53.610 --> 22:55.310
I thought you’d stop us.

22:55.310 --> 22:56.770
Why would we?

22:57.110 --> 23:00.280
Bike touring at night is a must-do!

23:00.280 --> 23:01.610
Go and have fun!

23:07.770 --> 23:10.600
Cynthia, take care of Haruno!

23:12.260 --> 23:15.120
Okay! Leave it to me!

23:15.120 --> 23:16.520
You’re going with that?

23:16.520 --> 23:17.370
I am!

23:17.640 --> 23:21.120
I use it every now and then,
so it’s ready to roll!

23:21.570 --> 23:24.520
Touring’s the most fun
when you ride together!

23:25.690 --> 23:28.470
Here we go!

23:29.570 --> 23:31.300
Be safe!

23:39.880 --> 23:41.730
It’s so dark that I can’t
see an inch ahead.

23:45.560 --> 23:49.030
But it’s not as scary as I thought.

23:50.850 --> 23:52.940
I’m with Cynthia, after all.

24:08.380 --> 24:12.590
This is too sharp! I can’t
go nearly as fast as I’d like.

24:14.900 --> 24:17.390
I’m doing fine?

24:17.590 --> 24:21.390
So it’s all right to go this slow!

24:21.390 --> 24:22.770
I just need to keep this up!

24:28.280 --> 24:31.030
You’re working hard, Giorno.

24:32.350 --> 24:35.800
<i>That depends on the person riding it.</i>

24:35.800 --> 24:38.990
<i>They said you used to say it all the time.</i>

24:41.530 --> 24:42.860
Are you really doing it?<i></i>

24:42.860 --> 24:43.770
Yeah!<i></i>

24:43.770 --> 24:45.560
But it’s all adults!<i></i>

24:45.560 --> 24:46.910
Can you really do it?<i></i>

24:46.910 --> 24:49.000
You never know unless you try!<i></i>

24:56.950 --> 25:00.520
How far I can go depends on me alone.

25:01.830 --> 25:06.440
Yeah, so if it’s impossible to begin with,

25:06.440 --> 25:08.700
why should I even bother trying?

25:09.430 --> 25:13.880
There are some things
I just can’t do by myself.

25:16.760 --> 25:18.740
How far have we come?

25:20.120 --> 25:23.440
No matter how many hills we ride over, the sea is nowhere to be seen.

25:23.440 --> 25:26.850
Let’s make this hill...

25:26.850 --> 25:28.780
the last.

25:38.370 --> 25:39.450
The sea.

25:45.850 --> 25:47.340
It’s the sea!

25:53.530 --> 25:55.190
It’s really the sea!

25:58.200 --> 25:58.990
No way.

25:59.690 --> 26:04.300
Wait, why am I crying?

26:05.940 --> 26:07.540
I don’t get it.

26:10.410 --> 26:13.690
This is great!

26:13.690 --> 26:16.280
Thank you, Cynthia!

26:17.510 --> 26:21.640
I never thought I could
really make it to the sea.

26:21.640 --> 26:23.350
It’s all thanks to you, Cynthia.

26:23.350 --> 26:26.640
Seriously? I helped you?

26:26.640 --> 26:28.870
Yeah, you did!

26:29.350 --> 26:32.280
Hurray! I did it!

26:32.280 --> 26:38.440
I realized yet again that
I can’t do anything on my own.

26:38.440 --> 26:40.520
I’m really grateful.

26:42.440 --> 26:48.010
I think that people like you, who can do anything alone, are amazing!

26:50.650 --> 26:52.280
You’re not alone.

26:54.550 --> 26:59.010
Neither am I, or anyone else. Nobody’s alone.

27:01.130 --> 27:03.520
Our bikes helped us,

27:03.520 --> 27:08.320
not to mention the people who made these bikes and the people who built the roads.

27:08.320 --> 27:13.000
Lots of people helped us come all this way.

27:17.320 --> 27:20.860
That’s how I always think
when I’m traveling.

27:21.270 --> 27:25.980
So many people I don’t
even know are helping me.

27:27.830 --> 27:32.340
That’s why I’m able to believe I can go anywhere, no matter how far.

27:36.180 --> 27:41.110
I think you should rely on others, too!

27:47.060 --> 27:49.880
Haruno, are you okay?

27:49.880 --> 27:51.950
It’s no biggie!

27:51.950 --> 27:54.100
Jeez, you’re soaked!

27:54.600 --> 27:57.300
Well, it’ll dry eventually.

27:57.970 --> 28:01.600
I can rely on others for help.

28:01.600 --> 28:07.740
That’s something I’ve
never considered before.

28:07.740 --> 28:09.840
“Nobody’s alone.”

28:10.410 --> 28:16.550
Those words, as though they were the closing words of a drama, echoed in my heart.

28:27.350 --> 28:32.730
fukaku iki wo suikonde miyou

28:27.350 --> 28:32.730
Try drawing a deep breath

28:35.690 --> 28:42.900
kata no chikara wo sotto nuite hora

28:35.690 --> 28:42.900
Just relax for a moment and see

28:43.780 --> 28:49.240
ookina koe de utatte miyou

28:43.780 --> 28:49.240
Try singing in a loud voice

28:52.080 --> 28:59.340
dareka ni kono uta ga todoku ka na

28:52.080 --> 28:59.340
Maybe the song will reach someone

28:59.380 --> 29:06.340
fukinukeru kaze no naka hitori

28:59.380 --> 29:06.340
I'm alone in the sharp wind

29:08.470 --> 29:16.690
iezu ni kakushiteta fuan mo aru kedo

29:08.470 --> 29:16.690
Hiding a few worries I couldn't say aloud

29:17.480 --> 29:25.860
te wo nobasou doko made mo tsuzuiteru

29:17.480 --> 29:25.860
Reach out and try to catch

29:26.910 --> 29:33.790
mabushii hikari wo tsukamaetara

29:26.910 --> 29:33.790
This bright light that just goes on forever

29:33.790 --> 29:42.840
arukidasou kono basho kara hajimeyou

29:33.790 --> 29:42.840
This is a good place to start walking

29:43.300 --> 29:55.060
dokoka de dareka ga kimi no koto matteru kara

29:43.300 --> 29:55.060
Someone somewhere is waiting for you
